import Json
import Optic
import Tagged
import Text
/-!
# Web.Loom

The Loom UI framework for Wiz: components, local state, typed event handlers,
keyed lists, a pure virtual DOM, deterministic server-side rendering (HTML strings),
and a keyed diff that produces small DOM patches. `web/framework/` has the browser
half (a patch applier and event delegation) and a demo.

The model is **VDOM, not fine-grained signals**, and it is chosen for the way the
existing web pages already work (web/Web.wiz, web/infoview.js):

* A page's state is a Wiz value held by JavaScript and handed back on every event
  (`wiz_web_step : state → event → state`). So the UI is a pure function
  `state → tree`, which is exactly what a virtual DOM wants. A signal graph would need
  a mutable heap, stable node identity and a subscription order that the step-function
  FFI does not have.
* The same `state → tree` function is the server-side renderer: `Loom.toHtml` is
  deterministic and needs no DOM, so `wiz doc` and the static pages can render a
  component tree without a browser.
* Keyed diffing is ~150 lines and has no runtime beyond the tree itself; a signal
  runtime (cells, dependency tracking, effect queue) would be larger in Wiz and would
  still need the diff for first paint.

Updates are **VDOM patches addressed by a child-index path** (`"0.2.1"`), through the
same `js_*` FFI the infoview uses: `Loom.patchesJson` gives JavaScript a list of
operations, and `web/framework/runtime.js` applies them. Nothing in this file is
`unsafe`, and no proof in it is evaluated natively (it trusts no native axiom).

## Components and local state

A component is a record of `init`, `update` and `view` (`Loom.Component`), with props
`P`, state `S` and messages `M`. Local state is addressed by a **lens**
(`lib/Optic.wiz`) into the application state: `useState` is a lens's `view`, `setState`
is its `over` (`Loom.useStateP`/`Loom.setStateP` on a `LensP`; the unsuffixed names are
the store-lens shims). Two components' lenses are disjoint paths, so their updates
commute (`Lens.Indep`, or `LensP.Indep`), and the lens laws give read-after-write. This
fits quantities: an ordinary component's state is unrestricted data at ω.

A component that owns a **one-shot resource** (an in-flight request, a focus lease)
uses `Loom.Owned S`: a linear state cell (quantity 1). Every step takes the token and
must return it, so the kernel rejects using it twice and rejects dropping it on a
branch -- `Loom.Owned` is the `Uniq` pattern of `lib/Region.wiz` without regions.

```
import Optic
import Web.Loom

inductive Msg where
  | inc
  | dec

structure Model where
  count : Nat

def countL : Lens Model Nat := fun s => (s.count, fun n => Model.mk n)

def view (s : Model) : Loom.VNode Msg :=
  Loom.el "div" [Loom.class "counter"]
    [Loom.on "click" Msg.inc (Loom.el "button" List.nil [Loom.text "+"]),
     Loom.text "count: ", Loom.text (Nat.toString s.count)]   -- `import IO` for Nat.toString

def app : Loom.App Model Msg := Loom.App.mk (Model.mk 0)
  (fun m s => match m with
    | .inc => Loom.setState countL Nat.succ s
    | .dec => Loom.setState countL (fun n => Nat.sub n 1) s)
  view

#eval (Loom.App.render app (Model.mk 2)).html   -- the HTML string
```
-/

-- ## Nodes

/-- An HTML attribute: a name and a value. Both are escaped when rendered. -/
def Loom.Attr : Type := String × String
/-- An attribute, `Loom.attr "class" "pane"`. -/
def Loom.attr (name value : String) : Loom.Attr := (name, value)
/-- The `class` attribute. -/
def Loom.class (value : String) : Loom.Attr := Loom.attr "class" value
/-- The `id` attribute. -/
def Loom.id (value : String) : Loom.Attr := Loom.attr "id" value

/-- A virtual node, as a first-child/next-sibling forest (Wiz has no nested inductive
types, so children are a `children` chain and a node's `next` is its following
sibling). Build nodes with the smart constructors below, which take ordinary `List`s
and always end a chain at `.nil`.

`on event msg node` attaches a typed message to `node`'s DOM `event` (`click`, `input`,
`keydown`, …); `render` numbers handlers in document order and dispatch passes the
message to the app's `update`. `raw html` inserts `html` unescaped: it is the one trust
boundary (see `Loom.raw`). -/
inductive Loom.VNode (M : Type) where
  | nil
  | text (s : String) (next : Loom.VNode M)
  | raw (html : String) (next : Loom.VNode M)
  | el (tag : String) (key : String) (attrs : List Loom.Attr) (children : Loom.VNode M) (next : Loom.VNode M)
  | on (event : String) (msg : M) (body : Loom.VNode M) (next : Loom.VNode M)
  | prevent (event : String) (msg : M) (body : Loom.VNode M) (next : Loom.VNode M)

/-- Put `rest` after the sibling chain `x`. -/
def Loom.append {M : Type} : Loom.VNode M → Loom.VNode M → Loom.VNode M
  | .nil, rest => rest
  | .text s n, rest => .text s (Loom.append n rest)
  | .raw h n, rest => .raw h (Loom.append n rest)
  | .el t k a cs n, rest => .el t k a cs (Loom.append n rest)
  | .on e m b n, rest => .on e m b (Loom.append n rest)
  | .prevent e m b n, rest => .prevent e m b (Loom.append n rest)

/-- `x` followed by the chain `rest`, merging two adjacent text nodes into one. HTML
merges adjacent text nodes when it parses a page, so the tree must merge them too: a
patch's child-index path addresses DOM nodes, and two text children would be one node
there. (Raw HTML is one element; see `Loom.raw`.) -/
def Loom.mergeText {M : Type} (x : Loom.VNode M) (rest : Loom.VNode M) : Loom.VNode M :=
  match x, rest with
  | .text a .nil, .text b r => .text (String.append a b) r
  | _, _ => Loom.append x rest

/-- A sibling chain from a list (adjacent text merged, as the DOM would). An empty text
node is dropped: it has no DOM node, so keeping it would make a patch path address a
node the DOM does not have (the playground's `#count` starts out empty). -/
def Loom.ofList {M : Type} : List (Loom.VNode M) → Loom.VNode M
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => match x with
    | .text s .nil => match String.isEmpty s with
      | .true => Loom.ofList xs
      | .false => Loom.mergeText x (Loom.ofList xs)
    | _ => Loom.mergeText x (Loom.ofList xs)

/-- A text node (escaped when rendered; a patch carries its unescaped text). -/
def Loom.text {M : Type} (s : String) : Loom.VNode M := .text s .nil
/-- Raw HTML, **not escaped**: only for output that is already trusted HTML (for
instance `TT.toHtml`, which escapes its own text). Every other text path escapes. -/
def Loom.raw {M : Type} (html : String) : Loom.VNode M := .raw html .nil
/-- An element: a tag, attributes and children. -/
def Loom.el {M : Type} (tag : String) (attrs : List Loom.Attr) (kids : List (Loom.VNode M)) : Loom.VNode M :=
  .el tag "" attrs (Loom.ofList kids) .nil
/-- A keyed element: its key is matched across renders when its siblings are reordered
(`Loom.diffChildren`). Only elements take keys; a key on anything else is ignored, and
keys must be unique among their siblings (a duplicate is matched to the first). -/
def Loom.keyed {M : Type} (key : String) (node : Loom.VNode M) : Loom.VNode M := match node with
  | .el t _ a cs n => .el t key a cs n
  | other => other
/-- Attach a message to a DOM event on `node`: one handler per event per element (the
last `on` for the same event wins, as in the DOM). -/
def Loom.on {M : Type} (event : String) (msg : M) (node : Loom.VNode M) : Loom.VNode M :=
  .on event msg node .nil

/-- Like `Loom.on`, but the handler decides whether the event's default action is
prevented: the element carries `data-wiz-prevent-EVENT`, and the driver asks the
runtime's `wiz_loom_consume` (an app's `Loom.LiveApp` policy) after the step. Use it for
a `keydown` on a textarea: a handler that prevents every key swallows typing, so the
runtime prevents only what it consumed (Ctrl/⌘+Enter, Save, …). A plain `Loom.on` keeps
the older rule (a handled event is prevented). -/
def Loom.onPrevent {M : Type} (event : String) (msg : M) (node : Loom.VNode M) : Loom.VNode M :=
  .prevent event msg node .nil
/-- A group of siblings, for a children list (do not use a group as one child). -/
def Loom.seq {M : Type} (kids : List (Loom.VNode M)) : Loom.VNode M := Loom.ofList kids

/-- Lift a component's view into a page's message type (Elm's `Html.map`): a child with
its own `Msg` composes into a page whose message type is larger, wrapping every handler's
message with `f`. Handler order and indices are the child's, so the patches do not move.
(`Loom.map` is the framework's list helper; this is the tree one.) -/
def Loom.mapMsg {A B : Type} (f : A → B) : Loom.VNode A → Loom.VNode B
  | .nil => .nil
  | .text s n => .text s (Loom.mapMsg f n)
  | .raw h n => .raw h (Loom.mapMsg f n)
  | .el t k a cs n => .el t k a (Loom.mapMsg f cs) (Loom.mapMsg f n)
  | .on e m b n => .on e (f m) (Loom.mapMsg f b) (Loom.mapMsg f n)
  | .prevent e m b n => .prevent e (f m) (Loom.mapMsg f b) (Loom.mapMsg f n)

-- ## Rendering

/-- The rendered tree: text is raw (escaped when written out), attributes are strings,
and event handlers have become `data-wiz-on-EVENT="index"` attributes. -/
inductive Loom.RNode where
  | nil
  | text (s : String) (next : Loom.RNode)
  | raw (html : String) (next : Loom.RNode)
  | el (tag : String) (key : String) (attrs : List Loom.Attr) (children : Loom.RNode) (next : Loom.RNode)

/-- Put `rest` after the sibling chain `x`. -/
def Loom.RNode.append : Loom.RNode → Loom.RNode → Loom.RNode
  | .nil, rest => rest
  | .text s n, rest => .text s (Loom.RNode.append n rest)
  | .raw h n, rest => .raw h (Loom.RNode.append n rest)
  | .el t k a cs n, rest => .el t k a cs (Loom.RNode.append n rest)

/-- A sibling chain from a list. -/
def Loom.RNode.ofList : List Loom.RNode → Loom.RNode
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => Loom.RNode.append x (Loom.RNode.ofList xs)

/-- The siblings of a rendered node, detached (each with no `next`). -/
def Loom.RNode.siblings : Loom.RNode → List Loom.RNode
  | .nil => .nil
  | .text s n => .cons (.text s .nil) (Loom.RNode.siblings n)
  | .raw h n => .cons (.raw h .nil) (Loom.RNode.siblings n)
  | .el t k a cs n => .cons (.el t k a cs .nil) (Loom.RNode.siblings n)

/-- The key of a rendered node (empty for text, raw text and unkeyed elements). -/
def Loom.RNode.key : Loom.RNode → String
  | .nil => ""
  | .text _ _ => ""
  | .raw _ _ => ""
  | .el _ k _ _ _ => k

/-- The state of a render: the output (reversed characters), the number of the next
handler, and the handlers so far (reversed). -/
structure Loom.Out (M : Type) where
  acc : List Char
  next : Nat
  handlers : List (String × M)

/-- Whether `s` is in `xs`. -/
def Loom.member (s : String) : List String → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons x xs => match String.eq s x with
    | .true => .true
    | .false => Loom.member s xs

/-- Void HTML elements: no closing tag. -/
def Loom.void (tag : String) : Bool :=
  Loom.member tag (List.cons "area" (List.cons "base" (List.cons "br" (List.cons "col"
    (List.cons "embed" (List.cons "hr" (List.cons "img" (List.cons "input" (List.cons "link"
      (List.cons "meta" (List.cons "param" (List.cons "source" (List.cons "track"
        (List.cons "wbr" List.nil))))))))))))))

/-- The attribute name of a handler: one attribute per event, so an element can carry a
`click` and a `keydown` handler at once (`data-wiz-on-click="0"`). -/
def Loom.eventAttr (event : String) : String := String.append "data-wiz-on-" event

/-- The `data-wiz-on-EVENT` value of a handler: its index in the rendered handler table. -/
def Loom.eventValue (index : Nat) : String :=
  String.mk (Json.natChars index [])

/-- The marker attribute of a handler that decides its own default action
(`Loom.onPrevent`): `data-wiz-prevent-EVENT`. -/
def Loom.preventAttr (event : String) : String := String.append "data-wiz-prevent-" event

/-- Attach the handler attribute for `event` (number `index`) and `extra` to the head of
`node`. Nested `on`s put more attributes on the same element; a text node is wrapped in
a `span` so that it has somewhere to carry the attribute. -/
def Loom.attachWith {M : Type} (event : String) (index : Nat) (extra : List Loom.Attr) :
    Loom.VNode M → Loom.VNode M
  | .el t k a cs n =>
    .el t k (List.append a (List.append [(Loom.attr (Loom.eventAttr event) (Loom.eventValue index))] extra)) cs n
  | .on e m b n => .on e m (Loom.attachWith event index extra b) n
  | .prevent e m b n => .prevent e m (Loom.attachWith event index extra b) n
  | .text s n => .el "span" "" (List.append [(Loom.attr (Loom.eventAttr event) (Loom.eventValue index))] extra) (.text s .nil) n
  | .raw h n => .el "span" "" (List.append [(Loom.attr (Loom.eventAttr event) (Loom.eventValue index))] extra) (.raw h .nil) n
  | .nil => .el "span" "" (List.append [(Loom.attr (Loom.eventAttr event) (Loom.eventValue index))] extra) .nil .nil

/-- Attach the handler attribute for `event` (number `index`) to the head of `node`. -/
def Loom.attach {M : Type} (event : String) (index : Nat) : Loom.VNode M → Loom.VNode M :=
  Loom.attachWith event index List.nil

/-- Attach the handler attribute and the "the runtime decides" marker. -/
def Loom.attachPrevent {M : Type} (event : String) (index : Nat) : Loom.VNode M → Loom.VNode M :=
  Loom.attachWith event index [(Loom.attr (Loom.preventAttr event) "1")]

/-- Turn a virtual tree into a rendered tree, numbering handlers in document order
(pre-order: the node's own handlers, then its children, then its next sibling). -/
partial def Loom.toR {M : Type} : Loom.VNode M → Loom.Out M → Loom.RNode × Loom.Out M
  | .nil, o => (.nil, o)
  | .text s n, o =>
    let r := Loom.toR n o;
    (.text s r.1, r.2)
  | .raw h n, o =>
    let r := Loom.toR n o;
    (.raw h r.1, r.2)
  | .el t k a cs n, o =>
    let rc := Loom.toR cs o;
    let rn := Loom.toR n rc.2;
    (.el t k a rc.1 rn.1, rn.2)
  | .on e m b n, o =>
    let index := o.next;
    let o1 : Loom.Out M := { o with next := index + 1, handlers := .cons (e, m) o.handlers };
    let r := Loom.toR (Loom.append (Loom.attach e index b) n) o1;
    (r.1, r.2)
  | .prevent e m b n, o =>
    let index := o.next;
    let o1 : Loom.Out M := { o with next := index + 1, handlers := .cons (e, m) o.handlers };
    let r := Loom.toR (Loom.append (Loom.attachPrevent e index b) n) o1;
    (r.1, r.2)

/-- An attribute's HTML: ` name="value"`, escaped. -/
def Loom.attrHtml (a : Loom.Attr) (h : Html) : Html :=
  Html.lit "\"" (Html.lit (Tagged.esc a.2) (Html.lit "=\"" (Html.lit a.1 (Html.lit " " h))))

/-- Attributes' HTML, left to right. -/
def Loom.attrsHtml : List Loom.Attr → Html → Html
  | .nil, h => h
  | .cons a rest, h => Loom.attrsHtml rest (Loom.attrHtml a h)

/-- An opening tag, `<tag attrs>`, before `h`. -/
def Loom.openTag (tag : String) (attrs : List Loom.Attr) (h : Html) : Html :=
  Html.lit ">" (Loom.attrsHtml attrs (Html.lit tag (Html.lit "<" h)))

/-- A closing tag, `</tag>`, before `h`. -/
def Loom.closeTag (tag : String) (h : Html) : Html :=
  Html.lit ">" (Html.lit tag (Html.lit "</" h))

/-- A rendered node and its following siblings, as HTML, before `h`. -/
def Loom.renderRNode : Loom.RNode → Html → Html
  | .nil, h => h
  | .text s n, h => Loom.renderRNode n (Html.lit (Tagged.esc s) h)
  | .raw r n, h => Loom.renderRNode n (Html.lit r h)
  | .el t k a cs n, h =>
    let opened := Loom.openTag t a h;
    match Loom.void t with
    | .true => Loom.renderRNode n opened
    | .false => Loom.renderRNode n (Loom.closeTag t (Loom.renderRNode cs opened))

/-- A rendered tree as an HTML string. -/
def Loom.htmlOf (n : Loom.RNode) : String := match Loom.renderRNode n (Html.mk [] 0) with
  | .mk acc _ => String.mk (List.revOnto acc [])

/-- A rendered view: its tree (for diffing), its HTML, and its handler table
(`event, message`, in document order). -/
structure Loom.Rendered (M : Type) where
  tree : Loom.RNode
  html : String
  handlers : List (String × M)

/-- Render a virtual tree: HTML for SSR, handlers for dispatch, and the tree for a
later `Loom.Rendered.diff`. Deterministic: no clock, no hashing, no allocation order. -/
def Loom.render {M : Type} (v : Loom.VNode M) : Loom.Rendered M :=
  let o : Loom.Out M := Loom.Out.mk [] 0 [];
  let r := Loom.toR v o;
  Loom.Rendered.mk r.1 (Loom.htmlOf r.1) (List.revOnto r.2.handlers [])

/-- A virtual tree as an HTML string (SSR). -/
def Loom.toHtml {M : Type} (v : Loom.VNode M) : String := (Loom.render v).html

-- ## Patches

/-- A DOM update. Paths are child indices from the container (text nodes count too):
`"0"` is the first child, `"0.2"` its third child, `""` the container itself.
`insert` takes HTML for a new child; `move` removes the child at `src` and reinserts it
so that it ends up at index `dst`; `remove` removes at `index`. -/
inductive Loom.Patch where
  | replace (path : String) (html : String)
  | text (path : String) (s : String)
  | setAttr (path : String) (name : String) (value : String)
  | removeAttr (path : String) (name : String)
  | insert (path : String) (index : Nat) (html : String)
  | remove (path : String) (index : Nat)
  | move (path : String) (src : Nat) (dst : Nat)

/-- The element at `n`, if any. -/
partial def Loom.at {A : Type} (n : Nat) : List A → Option A
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons x xs => match Nat.beq n 0 with
    | .true => .some x
    | .false => Loom.at (n - 1) xs

/-- The element at `n`, or `d`. -/
partial def Loom.atD {A : Type} (d : A) (n : Nat) : List A → A
  | .nil => d
  | .cons x xs => match Nat.beq n 0 with
    | .true => x
    | .false => Loom.atD d (n - 1) xs

/-- Insert `x` before position `n`. -/
partial def Loom.insertAt {A : Type} (n : Nat) (x : A) : List A → List A
  | .nil => .cons x .nil
  | .cons y ys => match Nat.beq n 0 with
    | .true => .cons x (.cons y ys)
    | .false => .cons y (Loom.insertAt (n - 1) x ys)

/-- Remove the element at `n`. -/
partial def Loom.removeAt {A : Type} (n : Nat) : List A → List A
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => match Nat.beq n 0 with
    | .true => xs
    | .false => .cons x (Loom.removeAt (n - 1) xs)

/-- Move the element at `src` so that it ends up at index `dst`. -/
def Loom.moveTo {A : Type} (src dst : Nat) (xs : List A) : List A :=
  match Loom.at src xs with
  | .some x => Loom.insertAt dst x (Loom.removeAt src xs)
  | .none => xs

/-- The key of the node; empty for text/raw. -/
def Loom.keyOf (n : Loom.RNode) : String := Loom.RNode.key n

/-- Whether the list has a key equal to `k`. -/
def Loom.hasKey (k : String) : List Loom.RNode → Bool
  | .nil => .false
  | .cons x xs => match String.eq (Loom.keyOf x) k with
    | .true => .true
    | .false => Loom.hasKey k xs

/-- The first index at or after `from` whose key is `k`. -/
partial def Loom.findKeyFrom (k : String) (from : Nat) : List Loom.RNode → Option Nat
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons x xs => match Nat.beq from 0 with
    | .true => match String.eq (Loom.keyOf x) k with
      | .true => .some 0
      | .false => (match Loom.findKeyFrom k 0 xs with
        | .some n => .some (n + 1)
        | .none => .none)
    | .false => (match Loom.findKeyFrom k (from - 1) xs with
      | .some n => .some (n + 1)
      | .none => .none)

/-- Whether every node in the list is an element with a non-empty key. -/
def Loom.allKeyed : List Loom.RNode → Bool
  | .nil => .true
  | .cons x xs => match String.eq (Loom.keyOf x) "" with
    | .true => .false
    | .false => Loom.allKeyed xs

/-- Whether the parent is the root (whose child paths have no leading dot). -/
def Loom.childPath (parent : String) (i : Nat) : String :=
  match String.eq parent "" with
  | .true => String.mk (Json.natChars i [])
  | .false => String.mk (List.append (String.chars parent)
      (List.append (String.chars ".") (Json.natChars i [])))

/-- An attribute's value by name. -/
def Loom.attrValue (name : String) : List Loom.Attr → Option String
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons a rest => match String.eq a.1 name with
    | .true => .some a.2
    | .false => Loom.attrValue name rest

/-- Remove the attributes of `old` that `new` does not have. -/
def Loom.removedAttrs (path : String) : List Loom.Attr → List Loom.Attr → List Loom.Patch
  | .nil, _ => []
  | .cons a rest, new => match Loom.attrValue a.1 new with
    | .some _ => Loom.removedAttrs path rest new
    | .none => .cons (.removeAttr path a.1) (Loom.removedAttrs path rest new)

/-- Set the attributes of `new` that are absent from `old` or have another value. -/
def Loom.setAttrs (path : String) (old : List Loom.Attr) : List Loom.Attr → List Loom.Patch
  | .nil => []
  | .cons a rest => match Loom.attrValue a.1 old with
    | .some v => match String.eq v a.2 with
      | .true => Loom.setAttrs path old rest
      | .false => .cons (.setAttr path a.1 a.2) (Loom.setAttrs path old rest)
    | .none => .cons (.setAttr path a.1 a.2) (Loom.setAttrs path old rest)

/-- Patches for the attributes: remove the ones that went away, set the new or changed
ones. -/
def Loom.diffAttrs (path : String) (old new : List Loom.Attr) : List Loom.Patch :=
  List.append (Loom.removedAttrs path old new) (Loom.setAttrs path old new)

-- (diffNode and diffChildren are mutual: an element's children are diffed by the same
-- function that diffs nodes.)

mutual
/-- Patches turning the node `old` into `new` at `path` (both are single nodes). -/
partial def Loom.diffNode (path : String) (old : Loom.RNode) (new : Loom.RNode) : List Loom.Patch :=
  match old, new with
  | .nil, .nil => []
  | .text s _, .text s' _ => match String.eq s s' with
    | .true => []
    | .false => [(.text path s')]
  | .raw h _, .raw h' _ => match String.eq h h' with
    | .true => []
    | .false => [(.replace path h')]
  | .el t k a cs _, .el t' k' a' cs' _ =>
    match String.eq t t' with
    | .false => [(.replace path (Loom.htmlOf new))]
    | .true => match String.eq k k' with
      | .false => [(.replace path (Loom.htmlOf new))]
      | .true => List.append (Loom.diffAttrs path a a')
          (Loom.diffChildren path (Loom.RNode.siblings cs) (Loom.RNode.siblings cs'))
  | _, _ => [(.replace path (Loom.htmlOf new))]

/-- Patches for a children list at `base` (which ends with `.`, or is empty at the
root): keyed when both lists are fully keyed, positional otherwise. -/
partial def Loom.diffChildren (base : String) (old new : List Loom.RNode) : List Loom.Patch :=
  match Loom.allKeyed old with
  | .true => match Loom.allKeyed new with
    | .true => Loom.diffKeyed base old new
    | .false => Loom.diffPositional base 0 old new
  | .false => Loom.diffPositional base 0 old new

/-- Positional diff: pair by index, then insert or remove at the tail. -/
partial def Loom.diffPositional (base : String) (i : Nat) : List Loom.RNode → List Loom.RNode → List Loom.Patch
  | .nil, .nil => []
  | .nil, .cons n ns =>
    .cons (.insert base i (Loom.htmlOf n)) (Loom.diffPositional base (i + 1) [] ns)
  | .cons o os, .nil =>
    .cons (.remove base i) (Loom.diffPositional base i os [])
  | .cons o os, .cons n ns =>
    List.append (Loom.diffNode (Loom.childPath base i) o n)
      (Loom.diffPositional base (i + 1) os ns)

/-- Keyed diff: drop the old children that are gone, then walk the new list, moving a
matching child into place (or inserting it), and finally remove the leftovers. -/
partial def Loom.diffKeyed (base : String) (old new : List Loom.RNode) : List Loom.Patch :=
  let kept := Loom.dropMissing base new 0 old;
  let walked := Loom.keyedLoop base 0 kept.1 new [];
  List.append kept.2 walked.2

/-- The old children still present in `new`, with `remove` patches for the others.
`j` is the child's current index (the number kept so far). -/
def Loom.dropMissing (base : String) (new : List Loom.RNode) (j : Nat) :
    List Loom.RNode → List Loom.RNode × List Loom.Patch
  | .nil => ([], [])
  | .cons o os =>
    match Loom.hasKey (Loom.keyOf o) new with
    | .true => let rest := Loom.dropMissing base new (j + 1) os; (.cons o rest.1, rest.2)
    | .false => let rest := Loom.dropMissing base new j os;
      (rest.1, .cons (.remove base j) rest.2)

/-- Walk `new` at index `i` over the current list `cur`, producing patches. -/
partial def Loom.keyedLoop (base : String) (i : Nat) (cur : List Loom.RNode) :
    List Loom.RNode → List Loom.Patch → List Loom.RNode × List Loom.Patch
  | .nil, acc => (cur, List.append acc (Loom.removeTail base i (List.length cur - i)))
  | .cons n ns, acc =>
    match Loom.at i cur with
    | .some c => match String.eq (Loom.keyOf c) (Loom.keyOf n) with
      | .true => Loom.keyedLoop base (i + 1) cur ns
          (List.append acc (Loom.diffNode (Loom.childPath base i) c n))
      | .false => match Loom.findKeyFrom (Loom.keyOf n) (i + 1) cur with
        | .some j => Loom.keyedLoop base (i + 1) (Loom.moveTo j i cur) ns
            (List.append acc (.cons (.move base j i)
              (Loom.diffNode (Loom.childPath base i) (Loom.atD n j cur) n)))
        | .none => Loom.keyedLoop base (i + 1) (Loom.insertAt i n cur) ns
            (List.append acc [(.insert base i (Loom.htmlOf n))])
    | .none => Loom.keyedLoop base (i + 1) (Loom.insertAt i n cur) ns
        (List.append acc [(.insert base i (Loom.htmlOf n))])

/-- Remove `k` children at index `i` (each removal shifts the next into place). -/
def Loom.removeTail (base : String) (i : Nat) : Nat → List Loom.Patch
  | .zero => []
  | .succ k => .cons (.remove base i) (Loom.removeTail base i k)
end

/-- Patches from one rendered view to another. -/
def Loom.Rendered.diff {M : Type} (old new : Loom.Rendered M) : List Loom.Patch :=
  Loom.diffChildren "" (Loom.RNode.siblings old.tree) (Loom.RNode.siblings new.tree)

-- ## JSON, for the browser half

/-- `map`, locally (the framework does not import lib/Text.wiz). -/
def Loom.map {A B : Type} (f : A → B) : List A → List B
  | .nil => .nil
  | .cons x xs => .cons (f x) (Loom.map f xs)

/-- One patch as JSON (`web/framework/runtime.js` applies it). -/
def Loom.Patch.toJson (p : Loom.Patch) : Json := match p with
  | .replace path html => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "replace"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "html" (Json.mkStr html)) List.nil)))
  | .text path s => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "text"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "text" (Json.mkStr s)) List.nil)))
  | .setAttr path name value => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "setAttr"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "name" (Json.mkStr name))
        (.cons (Json.field "value" (Json.mkStr value)) List.nil))))
  | .removeAttr path name => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "removeAttr"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "name" (Json.mkStr name)) List.nil)))
  | .insert path index html => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "insert"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "index" (Json.ofNat index))
        (.cons (Json.field "html" (Json.mkStr html)) List.nil))))
  | .remove path index => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "remove"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "index" (Json.ofNat index)) List.nil)))
  | .move path src dst => Json.mkObj (.cons (Json.field "op" (Json.mkStr "move"))
      (.cons (Json.field "path" (Json.mkStr path)) (.cons (Json.field "src" (Json.ofNat src))
        (.cons (Json.field "dst" (Json.ofNat dst)) List.nil))))

/-- A patch list as JSON, for `js_patch`. -/
def Loom.patchesJson (ps : List Loom.Patch) : String :=
  Json.render (Json.mkArr (Loom.map Loom.Patch.toJson ps))

-- ## Components, state, dispatch

/-- Read a component's local state at a profunctor lens: `useState` is `view`. -/
def Loom.useStateP {S : Type} {ω A : Type} (l : LensP S S A A) (s : S) : A := view l s
/-- Update a component's local state at a profunctor lens: `setState` is `over`. The lens
laws (`LensP.GetPut`, `LensP.PutGet`) give read-after-write; two components' lenses on
independent paths commute (`LensP.Indep`, which a derived `Lens.Indep` supplies through
`LensP.ofLens_indep`). -/
def Loom.setStateP {S : Type} {ω A : Type} (l : LensP S S A A) (f : A → A) (s : S) : S := over l f s
/-- A reducer on a component's local state (`useReducer`), at a profunctor lens. -/
def Loom.useReducerP {S : Type} {ω A : Type} {M : Type} (l : LensP S S A A) (step : M → A → A) (m : M) (s : S) : S :=
  over l (step m) s

/-- Read a component's local state: `useState` is a lens's get (the store-lens shim of
`Loom.useStateP`, so `deriving Lens` fields work unchanged). -/
def Loom.useState {S : Type} {ω A : Type} (l : Lens S A) (s : S) : A :=
  let lp : LensP S S A A := LensP.ofLens l;
  Loom.useStateP lp s
/-- Update a component's local state: `setState` is a lens's over. The lens laws
(`Lens.GetPut`, `Lens.PutGet`) give read-after-write; two components' lenses on
independent paths commute (`Lens.Indep`). -/
def Loom.setState {S : Type} {ω A : Type} (l : Lens S A) (f : A → A) (s : S) : S :=
  let lp : LensP S S A A := LensP.ofLens l;
  Loom.setStateP lp f s
/-- A reducer on a component's local state (`useReducer`). -/
def Loom.useReducer {S : Type} {ω A : Type} {M : Type} (l : Lens S A) (step : M → A → A) (m : M) (s : S) : S :=
  let lp : LensP S S A A := LensP.ofLens l;
  Loom.useReducerP lp step m s

/-- A component: its initial state from props, its update, and its view. -/
structure Loom.Component (P S M : Type) where
  init : P → S
  update : M → S → S
  view : P → S → Loom.VNode M

/-- Render a component (`props`, `state`) to a `Rendered`. -/
def Loom.Component.render {P S M : Type} (c : Loom.Component P S M) (p : P) (s : S) : Loom.Rendered M :=
  Loom.render (c.view p s)

/-- A whole app: initial state, update and view. -/
structure Loom.App (S M : Type) where
  init : S
  update : M → S → S
  view : S → Loom.VNode M

/-- The app's view at `s`, rendered. -/
def Loom.App.render {S M : Type} (a : Loom.App S M) (s : S) : Loom.Rendered M :=
  Loom.render (a.view s)

/-- SSR: the app at `s` as HTML. -/
def Loom.App.html {S M : Type} (a : Loom.App S M) (s : S) : String := (Loom.App.render a s).html

/-- The message of handler `i` (document order), if any. -/
partial def Loom.handlerAt {M : Type} (i : Nat) : List (String × M) → Option M
  | .nil => .none
  | .cons h hs => match Nat.beq i 0 with
    | .true => .some h.2
    | .false => Loom.handlerAt (i - 1) hs

/-- Dispatch handler `i` (the browser sends its `data-wiz-on-EVENT` index): the next state. -/
def Loom.App.dispatch {S M : Type} (a : Loom.App S M) (s : S) (i : Nat) : S :=
  match Loom.handlerAt i (Loom.App.render a s).handlers with
  | .some m => a.update m s
  | .none => s

/-- Dispatch only if the handler's event name is `event` (the browser sends both, so a
stale index from a previous render cannot fire the wrong message). -/
def Loom.App.event {S M : Type} (a : Loom.App S M) (s : S) (event : String) (i : Nat) : S :=
  match Loom.at i (Loom.App.render a s).handlers with
  | .some h => match String.eq h.1 event with
    | .true => a.update h.2 s
    | .false => s
  | .none => s

/-- The patches from the app's state `s` to `s'` (render both, keyed-diff). -/
def Loom.App.patch {S M : Type} (a : Loom.App S M) (s s' : S) : List Loom.Patch :=
  Loom.Rendered.diff (Loom.App.render a s) (Loom.App.render a s')

/-- `Loom.App.patch` as JSON, for `js_patch`. -/
def Loom.App.patches {S M : Type} (a : Loom.App S M) (s s' : S) : String :=
  Loom.patchesJson (Loom.App.patch a s s')

-- ## Events with a payload (form controls, keys)

/-- One browser event: the DOM type, the handler index that answered it, and the payload
`web/framework/driver.js` attached (a form control's value for `input`/`change`, the key
for `keydown`/`keyup`; empty for the rest). -/
structure Loom.Event where
  name : String
  index : Nat
  payload : String

/-- A decimal string as a number (`0` when it is not one). -/
def Loom.natOr0 (s : String) : Nat := match String.parseNat s with
  | .some n => n
  | .none => 0

/-- Split the driver's event string. The driver sends `event "\n" index "\n" payload`, and
the payload is the rest of the string, so a textarea's newlines arrive intact:
`"input\n3\na\nb"` is `input`, handler 3, `"a\nb"`. -/
def Loom.splitEvent (s : String) : Loom.Event :=
  match String.splitOn s "\n" with
  | .nil => Loom.Event.mk "" 0 ""
  | .cons name rest => match rest with
    | .nil => Loom.Event.mk name 0 ""
    | .cons index tail => Loom.Event.mk name (Loom.natOr0 index) (String.intercalate "\n" tail)

/-- An app whose messages carry the event's payload: `update msg payload state`. Use it
when a view binds a form control (`input`/`change`) or a key (`keydown`/`keyup`); a
`Loom.App` whose messages need no payload stays as it is. -/
structure Loom.LiveApp (S M : Type) where
  init : S
  update : M → String → S → S
  view : S → Loom.VNode M

/-- The app's view at `s`, rendered. -/
def Loom.LiveApp.render {S M : Type} (a : Loom.LiveApp S M) (s : S) : Loom.Rendered M :=
  Loom.render (a.view s)

/-- SSR: the app at `s` as HTML. -/
def Loom.LiveApp.html {S M : Type} (a : Loom.LiveApp S M) (s : S) : String :=
  (Loom.LiveApp.render a s).html

/-- The patches from the app's state `s` to `s'`. -/
def Loom.LiveApp.patch {S M : Type} (a : Loom.LiveApp S M) (s s' : S) : List Loom.Patch :=
  Loom.Rendered.diff (Loom.LiveApp.render a s) (Loom.LiveApp.render a s')

/-- `Loom.LiveApp.patch` as JSON, for `js_patch`. -/
def Loom.LiveApp.patches {S M : Type} (a : Loom.LiveApp S M) (s s' : S) : String :=
  Loom.patchesJson (Loom.LiveApp.patch a s s')

/-- Dispatch one browser event string (`Loom.splitEvent`), giving the message its
payload. A stale index from a previous render cannot fire the wrong message: the event
name has to match the handler's too. -/
def Loom.LiveApp.step {S M : Type} (a : Loom.LiveApp S M) (s : S) (ev : String) : S :=
  let e := Loom.splitEvent ev;
  match Loom.at e.index (Loom.LiveApp.render a s).handlers with
  | .some h => match String.eq h.1 e.name with
    | .true => a.update h.2 e.payload s
    | .false => s
  | .none => s

-- ## Owned (linear) state

/-- A one-shot state cell: the token is used at quantity 1, so the kernel rejects
using it twice and rejects dropping it. The state itself is ordinary (ω) data, as in
`Uniq`. Only this module constructs it (`private mk`). -/
inductive Loom.Owned (S : Type) where
  | private mk (state : S)

/-- A new one-shot cell. -/
def Loom.Owned.new {S : Type} (s : S) : Loom.Owned S := Loom.Owned.mk s

/-- Use the cell once: run `k` on the state and return its result. -/
def Loom.Owned.read {S B : Type} (1 o : Loom.Owned S) (k : S → B) : B :=
  match o with
  | .mk s => k s

/-- The state, and the cell back (`*o` in direct style). -/
def Loom.Owned.peek {S : Type} (1 o : Loom.Owned S) : S × Loom.Owned S :=
  match o with
  | .mk s => (s, Loom.Owned.mk s)

/-- Update the state, giving the cell back. -/
def Loom.Owned.update {S : Type} (1 o : Loom.Owned S) (f : S → S) : Loom.Owned S :=
  match o with
  | .mk s => Loom.Owned.mk (f s)

/-- Replace the state, giving the cell back. -/
def Loom.Owned.set {S : Type} (1 o : Loom.Owned S) (s : S) : Loom.Owned S :=
  match o with
  | .mk _ => Loom.Owned.mk s

/-- End the one-shot state: its final value (the only way to discard the cell, and it
must be written on every path). -/
def Loom.Owned.end {S : Type} (1 o : Loom.Owned S) : S :=
  match o with
  | .mk s => s

attribute [inline] Loom.Owned.new
attribute [inline] Loom.Owned.read
attribute [inline] Loom.Owned.peek
attribute [inline] Loom.Owned.update
attribute [inline] Loom.Owned.set
attribute [inline] Loom.Owned.end
